Severity: FAIL
Category: network
Check: check_ntp

The NTP daemon is running but its configuration restricts none of its
remote servers, so any of them may reconfigure it. A rogue or
compromised server can then shift the clock or turn the daemon into an
amplifier for others. Add a "restrict" line for every server (and a
"default ignore" style default where the daemon supports it) and
restart it.
